%T A395680 1,1,0,1,1,0,8,6,7,2,5,4,1,7,2,7,1,6,1,3,4,0,6,9,3,2,2,5,0,1,8,7,3,6,
%U A395680 4,0,8,7,8,5,0,7,2,4,7,8,3,3,2,8,1
%N A395680 Decimal expansion of the constant d = Product_{n>=0} (1 - 1/(2*n!+1)).
%C A395680 This constant arises in three geometric contexts:
%C A395680 (1) Stochastic geometry: probability a point on a circle is never covered when, at level n, an arc of angular measure 2*Pi/(2*n!+1) is placed at an independent uniformly random position on the circle - the vacancy (void) probability of a Dvoretzky-type random covering process.
%C A395680 (2) Combinatorial geometry: consider a hierarchy of regular polygons where the polygon at level n has 2*n! ordinary vertices and 1 marked vertex, equally spaced on a circle. d is the probability that a uniformly random vertex is never the marked one, across the entire hierarchy of polygon sizes.
%C A395680 (3) Algebraic geometry: consider a hierarchy where, at level n, the discriminant-complement configuration space of n labeled roots of a generic degree-n polynomial (an S_n-cover of order n!, doubled by an independent choice of square-root branch) has 2*n! ordinary sheets and 1 marked sheet. d is the probability that a uniformly random sheet is never the marked one, across the entire hierarchy of degrees.
%F A395680 Equals Product_{n>=0} (1 - 1/(2*n!+1)).
%F A395680 Satisfies -log(d) = Sum_{k>=1} D_k/k, where D_k = Sum_{n>=0} 1/(2*n!+1)^k and D_1 = D (A396384).
%e A395680 d = (2/3)*(2/3)*(4/5)*(12/13)*(48/49)*... = 0.31991462763026131388299222883...
%t A395680 N[Product[1-1/(2*n!+1), {n, 0, Infinity}], 50]
%o A395680 (Python)
%o A395680 from mpmath import mp, nprod, factorial, inf
%o A395680 mp.dps = 50
%o A395680 print(nprod(lambda n: 1-1/(2*factorial(n)+1), [0, inf]))
%o A395680 (PARI) prodinf(k=0, 1-1/(2*k!+1))
%Y A395680 Cf. A396384 (D), A000142.
%K A395680 nonn,cons
%O A395680 0,1
